# ASTROWORLD — Project Rules

Mobile-first social app for amateur astronomers. Frontend phase: build screens on MOCK DATA only. No backend yet.

## Stack (fixed — do not substitute or add libraries without asking)
- Expo (React Native), SDK 54
- TypeScript
- Expo Router (file-based routing in /app)
- TanStack Query (server state — not used until backend phase)
- Zustand (local state)
- NativeWind (styling)
- Reanimated (animation)
- react-native-maps (terrestrial maps only)
- Sentry (error tracking)

## Project structure
- /app — routes/screens. Logic, data, state, navigation ONLY. No raw styling.
- /components/ui — presentational ("dumb") components. The ONLY place styling lives.
- /lib — types, helpers
- /mocks — typed mock data + sync accessor functions (stand-in for real data)
- /store — Zustand stores
- /theme — design tokens

## Separation of logic and presentation (so Figma designs can drop in later)
- Screens compose /components/ui primitives. They never style directly, never use inline styles, never hardcode visual values.
- Presentational components receive everything via typed props. No business logic, no data fetching, no store access inside them.
- Every component has its own file with an exported typed props interface.
- All UI imports come from the barrel: `import { Card, Button } from '@/components/ui'`. Never import UI from individual files.
- Keep exported names and prop shapes stable — this barrel is the swap point for future Figma-based implementations.

## Theme (Aurora) — use tokens, never hardcode these values
- bg #000000 · surface #23313e · teal #86cdc3 · lavender #bb90e3 · blue #52a5dc · text #ecf3f2 · muted #bac7d2
- All color/spacing/radius/font values reference /theme tokens, not literals in components.
- Red-light mode: when enabled, swap to red-only palette (dark red bg, red text/accents, NO blue/green/white).

## Data (frontend phase)
- All data is mock data from /mocks via synchronous accessor functions (e.g. getMockSessions()).
- No network calls, no Supabase, no auth. Mock accessors are the seams where real data plugs in later.

## Design principles
- Calm, not addictive: no infinite-scroll dopamine loops, restrained animation.
- Field-ready: core flows (logging, saved plans) work with zero network by design.
- Built by stargazers: correct astronomy vocabulary, no condescension, no salesman tone.

## Workflow
- Build only what the current prompt asks. Stop and summarize when done.
- Keep diffs small and reviewable. Don't refactor unrelated code.
- If a needed UI component doesn't exist, create it in /components/ui first, then consume it.

## Quality gates (run after EVERY change, do not proceed until clean)
- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes
- linter passes
- never log user PII to Sentry
